---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="AHGlasses | Projects | Wretzelectronics">
  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="detail-header">
      <h1 class="project-title">AHGlasses</h1>
      <p class="project-tagline">Wearable real-time OCR and speech-to-text subtitle system.</p>
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag-badge">Pi Zero W</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">Vosk Speech Engine</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">Tesseract OCR</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">HTML Overlay</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="hero-image-wrapper">
      <img src="/images/projects/ahglasses.png" alt="AHGlasses wearable rig" class="detail-hero-img" />
    </div>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        AHGlasses is a wearable system that provides real-time OCR and speech-to-text subtitles
        using a Pi Zero W capture node and a laptop processing pipeline. The project explores
        lightweight wearable capture, heterogeneous processing, and responsive subtitle display
        through a browser-based UI.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        AHGlasses uses a dual-processor architecture: the Pi Zero W handles camera capture while
        the laptop performs OCR, speech recognition, and output coordination. This inverted model
        contrasts with AHGadget, where the Pi handled most of the computation.
      </p>

      <div class="diagram-block">
        <h3>System Architecture Diagram</h3>
        <p class="diagram-caption">High-level view of camera, microphone, server, and subtitle web renderer.</p>
        <img src="/images/projects/ahglasses-architecture.png" alt="AHGlasses architecture diagram" class="diagram-img" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Processing Pipeline</h2>
      <p>
        The pipeline integrates camera capture, microphone input, OCR preprocessing, Vosk speech
        recognition, and HTML overlay rendering.
      </p>

      <div class="diagram-block">
        <h3>Data Flow / Pipeline Diagram</h3>
        <p class="diagram-caption">Subsystem data processing sequence from capture to live web overlay.</p>
        <img src="/images/projects/ahglasses-pipeline.png" alt="AHGlasses data flow pipeline" class="diagram-img" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>User Interface</h2>
      <p>
        The browser-based UI displays OCR and speech recognition results as live subtitles. It is
        lightweight, responsive, and designed for real-world environments with variable lighting
        and noise.
      </p>

      <div class="diagram-block">
        <h3>Subtitle Display</h3>
        <p class="diagram-caption">HTML overlay presenting live OCR and speech-to-text text streams.</p>
        <img src="/images/projects/ahglasses-ui.png" alt="AHGlasses subtitle UI" class="diagram-img" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Development Notes</h2>
      <p>
        Development focused on stabilizing the laptop-side pipeline, improving OCR preprocessing,
        handling noisy audio environments, and balancing responsiveness with accuracy.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project-detail {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .detail-header {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .project-tagline {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tag-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .hero-image-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.2);
    background: #000;
  }

  .detail-hero-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 480px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .content-section p {
    color: var(--text-main);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .diagram-block {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .diagram-block h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--border-neon);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .diagram-caption {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem !important;
  }

  .diagram-img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    background: #000;
    display: block;
  }
</style>